Name: Error Prone
Short Name: Error Prone
Version: N/A
Revision: DEPS
Update Mechanism: Autoroll
License: Apache-2.0, MIT
License File: LICENSE, LICENSE.nullaway
Security Critical: No
Shipped: no
URL: https://errorprone.info/

Description:
Java static analysis tool.

The CIPD package contains:
 * error_prone_core.jar: Error Prone and its dependencies.
 * nullaway.jar: NullAway (https://github.com/uber/NullAway/), an Error Prone
   plugin for checking @Nullable annotations (MIT license). Classes that already
   exist in error_prone_core.jar are removed.
 * NULLAWAY_VERSION: The version of NullAway within nullaway.jar.
 * error_prone: A GraalVM native-image (linux-x64 only) of javac with Error
   Prone, NullAway, and //tools/android/errorprone_plugin compiled in. Built
   with Oracle GraalVM, which is licensed under the GraalVM Free Terms and
   Conditions.

Local Modifications:
None

What version is this:
  * Run print_version.sh to find out the version.
  * The NullAway version is in cipd/NULLAWAY_VERSION. NullAway is updated
    whenever a new Error Prone package is built.
  * New instances are uploaded by the packager bot:
    https://ci.chromium.org/p/chromium/builders/ci/3pp-linux-amd64-packager
  * The bot autoruns every 6 hours. Ping a trooper or a clank-build-core@ dev to
    trigger it if you need it sooner:
    https://luci-scheduler.appspot.com/jobs/chromium/3pp-linux-amd64-packager
  * New versions are rolled automatically by:
    TODO(agrieve): Add auto-roller.

Tips on Rolling:
NullAway is rolled along with Error Prone. If there are a lot of new NullAway
warnings, suppress them by:

1) Create a copy / paste of NullAway.assumeNonNull() (e.g. "suppressNullAway")
2) Update errorprone.py:
   -ERRORPRONE_CHECKS_TO_APPLY = []
   +ERRORPRONE_CHECKS_TO_APPLY = ['NullAway']
   ...
   +    errorprone_flags += ['-XepOpt:NullAway:SuggestSuppressions=true']
   ..
   -                          'org.chromium.build.NullUtil.assumeNonNull')]
   +                          'org.chromium.build.NullUtil.suppressNullAway')]
3) Update build/config/siso/android.star (for "android/errorprone" block):
   +            "remote": False,
4) Build all targets: cd out/Debug && ../../tools/android/build_all_errorprone.sh
